 30, 2026. Tanger Inc. was established in 1981 and was incorporated in North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen J. Yalof | President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 407 people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $726K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $31K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Tanger Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $4.7B market cap on $582M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 69% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $295M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 51 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.57\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 63/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 16% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (SKT) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_SKT_Movement_111326022602_1794597962.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794597962.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Tanger (SKT)'s Raised Earnings Guidance Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-skt/tanger/news/what-tanger-skts-raised-earnings-guidance-means-for-sharehol","